{"type":"message","id":"2d18c427","parentId":"8d348c06","timestamp":"2026-06-24T08:28:22.663Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_rwore8uqejyn_1","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/vhallac/semblr/issues/86\",\n  \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/vhallac/semblr\",\n  \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/vhallac/semblr/issues/86/labels{/name}\",\n  \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/vhallac/semblr/issues/86/comments\",\n  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/vhallac/semblr/issues/86/events\",\n  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/vhallac/semblr/issues/86\",\n  \"id\": 4722537777,\n  \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOSoADIs8AAAABGXw1MQ\",\n  \"number\": 86,\n  \"title\": \"Adapt sakana.ai's TRINITY into multi-model routing\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"login\": \"vhallac\",\n    \"id\": 93108,\n    \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjkzMTA4\",\n    \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93108?v=4\",\n    \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/vhallac\",\n    \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac/followers\",\n    \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac/following{/other_user}\",\n    \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac/gists{/gist_id}\",\n    \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n    \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac/subscriptions\",\n    \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac/orgs\",\n    \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac/repos\",\n    \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac/events{/privacy}\",\n    \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/vhallac/received_events\",\n    \"type\": \"User\",\n    \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n    \"site_admin\": false\n  },\n  \"labels\": [\n\n  ],\n  \"state\": \"open\",\n  \"locked\": false,\n  \"assignees\": [\n\n  ],\n  \"milestone\": null,\n  \"comments\": 2,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-06-23T04:08:06Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-24T05:42:04Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": null,\n  \"assignee\": null,\n  \"author_association\": \"OWNER\",\n  \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n  \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n    \"total\": 0,\n    \"completed\": 0,\n    \"percent_completed\": 0\n  },\n  \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n    \"blocked_by\": 0,\n    \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n    \"blocking\": 0,\n    \"total_blocking\": 0\n  },\n  \"body\": \"# Background\\n\\nVery broadly speaking and overlooking the fine details; TRINITY is a small classifier network that creates a \\\"hidden state\\\", and decides which of the three backend models should address this turn. It also embeds a small prompt into the turn start: the chosen model receives: previous tokens of round, tool results, and the prompt (probably pre-cooked prompt selected by the network - TRINITY is NOT an LLM).\\n\\n# Idea\\n\\nThis mechanism is very similar to what semblr does for clipping extremely long rounds: injecting a prompt to get the LLMM to summarize and wrap up.\\n\\nWe can get the LLM itself to report its round status via a dedicated tool in semblr, and route the conversation to another model. This is essentially the same mechanism, but instead of a context size threshold with no intelligence, semblr can outsource the necessary intelligence to the called LLM. The tool call can have at least one parameter: upcoming generation phase. One possible set is as listed below.\\n\\n- exploring — I'm still decomposing, keep me on this model\\n- executing — I have a clear plan, maybe switch to a faster/cheaper Worker\\n- stuck — I've been going in circles, escalate or swap\\n- verifying — I've produced something, bring in a different model to check it\\n- done — collapse the chain\\n\\nAnother parameter is a \\\"note to future self\\\".\\n\\n# Problems\\n\\nThis is hard to get right: the LLM needs to decide when it will change mode of generation (context gathering, exploring, fact collection, planning, etc.) and report it. There is no prior art to this; and the whole \\\"report your next step to me\\\" idea may fail.\\n\\nWeaker models we want to use for routine operations may be too weak to utilize this effectively, getting stuck in an early mode.\\n\\nAnother complication is pi coding agent: it may prevent us from switching models mid-generation.\\n\\nFinally, every model switch will create uncached tokens. Increasing the cost of generation.\",\n  \"closed_by\": null,\n  \"reactions\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/vhallac/semblr/issues/86/reactions\",\n    \"total_count\": 0,\n    \"+1\": 0,\n    \"-1\": 0,\n    \"laugh\": 0,\n    \"hooray\": 0,\n    \"confused\": 0,\n    \"heart\": 0,\n    \"rocket\": 0,\n    \"eyes\": 0\n  },\n  \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/vhallac/semblr/issues/86/timeline\",\n  \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n  \"state_reason\": null,\n  \"pinned_comment\": null\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1782289702663}}
